; The flags of every library, test and bench under packages/nx. A stanza names
; no flag of its own.
;
; Since dune language 3.21 the dev profile compiles with the compiler's
; default warnings, which leave unused values, opens and fields unreported:
; keep dune's stricter development set. A C warning is an error in every
; profile but release: a release build must not break on a warning a future
; compiler adds.
;
; Every profile but sanitize compiles the C at -O3, so that the benches and
; tests run the code a release build ships. Against -O2, gcc's -O3 ran the
; kernel and nx bench rows in 0.88 of the time on the M1 under Homebrew's
; gcc 15 (geomean; a float32 sum 5 times as fast; Apple's cc is clang),
; 0.975 on an Arrow Lake's base table and 1.00 on its v3 table; clang's
; ran them within 1%. The sanitize profile keeps :standard's level: it
; runs tests, never benches, and less inlining keeps its reports' stack
; traces closer to the source.
;
; Every profile passes -ffp-contract=off, so that a compiler never fuses a
; multiply and an add. No codec has a product that feeds a sum:
; nx_mini_value's products are exact scalings by powers of two. The flag
; keeps an exact identity that needs one from being fused.
;
; Every profile also passes -fno-trapping-math and -fno-math-errno, which
; change no value: no code here enables a floating-point trap or reads errno.
; Without them gcc vectorises neither a codec that selects between results of
; float operations, since one might trap, nor a loop that calls a libm
; function such as sqrt, which may set errno.
;
; The sanitize profile compiles the C with AddressSanitizer and
; UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer and links their runtimes and the debug runtime
; into every executable: a report ends the process, and the collector runs
; often enough that a value a stub holds unrooted fails at once. Against
; rig's options (packages/rig/dune), the minor heap is 256 KiB (s=32k) and
; no heap check ends a major cycle. A minor collection stops every domain,
; and on a machine with fewer free cores than a test's domains it waits for
; each to be scheduled: under 32 KiB the two-domain tests of donation ran 4
; to 5 times as long beside two busy processes on three cores, and timed
; out. A heap check walks the whole heap, and the suites whose references
; hold hundreds of thousands of values ran 5 to 20 times as long, past
; their time. v=0 silences the debug runtime's messages, which an expect
; test would read as output.
;
; Benches are not attached to runtest: run them with `dune build @bench`, or
; run a built exe from its directory under _build/default. Every bench rule
; takes the workspace lock %{workspace_root}/bench.

(env
 (release
  (c_flags
   (:standard
    -std=c11
    -O3
    -ffp-contract=off
    -fno-trapping-math
    -fno-math-errno
    -Wall
    -Wextra))
  (env-vars
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60)))
 (sanitize
  (c_flags
   (:standard
    -std=c11
    -ffp-contract=off
    -fno-trapping-math
    -fno-math-errno
    -Wall
    -Wextra
    -Werror
    -g
    -fno-omit-frame-pointer
    -fsanitize=address,undefined))
  (link_flags
   (:standard -runtime-variant d -cclib -fsanitize=address,undefined))
  (env-vars
   (OCAMLRUNPARAM s=32k,o=20,M=1,m=1,v=0)
   (ASAN_OPTIONS
    halt_on_error=1:detect_leaks=0:use_sigaltstack=0:allocator_may_return_null=1)
   (UBSAN_OPTIONS halt_on_error=1:print_stacktrace=1)
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60)))
 (dev
  (flags
   (:standard %{dune-warnings}))
  (c_flags
   (:standard
    -std=c11
    -O3
    -ffp-contract=off
    -fno-trapping-math
    -fno-math-errno
    -Wall
    -Wextra
    -Werror))
  (env-vars
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60)))
 (_
  (c_flags
   (:standard
    -std=c11
    -O3
    -ffp-contract=off
    -fno-trapping-math
    -fno-math-errno
    -Wall
    -Wextra
    -Werror))
  (env-vars
   (WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT 60))))
